$ErrorActionPreference='Stop'
$Here=Split-Path -Parent $MyInvocation.MyCommand.Path
$Source=Join-Path $Here 'staged'
$Updates=Join-Path $Here 'distribution\updates'
$Version=(Get-Content -Raw (Join-Path $Source 'app\release_info.json') | ConvertFrom-Json).app_version
$Exclude=@('tests','archive','distribution','.venv','__pycache__')
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force -Path $Updates|Out-Null
$Stage=Join-Path $Updates 'LabTools'
if(Test-Path $Stage){Remove-Item -LiteralPath $Stage -Recurse -Force}
Copy-Item -LiteralPath $Source -Destination $Stage -Recurse
Get-ChildItem -LiteralPath $Stage -Directory -Recurse -Force|
 Where-Object{$_.Name-in$Exclude}|Sort-Object FullName -Descending|
 Remove-Item -Recurse -Force
$Zip=Join-Path $Updates "WINK_App_Update_v$Version.zip"
if(Test-Path $Zip){Remove-Item -LiteralPath $Zip -Force}
Compress-Archive -LiteralPath $Stage -DestinationPath $Zip -CompressionLevel Optimal
$Hash=(Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 -LiteralPath $Zip).Hash.ToLowerInvariant()
[ordered]@{
 app_version=$Version
 package_filename=(Split-Path -Leaf $Zip)
 package_sha256=$Hash
 min_runtime_version='1.0.0'
 changelog='v11.116 Population swimming is renamed Population tracking, its review now happens inside the tool window over the movie, and eight defects were fixed. IMPORTANT: re-analysing a recording used to silently show you the PREVIOUS run. Results land in a folder named after the recording, and the review preferred the earlier reviewed file over the detections just computed - so changing area gates, resolution or ROIs appeared to do nothing. On a real recording a fresh 5.8 MB detection set (about 20,000 rows) was discarded in favour of a 176 KB leftover holding 432 rows. A new analysis now archives any previous review into superseded_review_<timestamp>/ and uses the fresh detections; Resume existing results review still restores prior work. Also fixed: the spine skeletoniser could loop forever at 100% CPU on any mask that filled its own bounding box (reachable whenever a low-resolution proxy admitted tiny solid blobs), which is why runs sat on one track for 20+ minutes; the bout review Confirm/Relabel/Reject buttons silently did nothing on pandas 3 because an empty label column was read as float; Tk callback errors vanished into stderr and are now reported in the hood with file and line; and the tracker could weld separate animals into one track because it extrapolated position by velocity across long crossing holds - a link must now also satisfy a physical speed limit from the last OBSERVED position, and Max link is exposed (measured worm motion on a 4K recording is about 2-6 px per frame against a hard-coded gate of 60). Review is now one window instead of four: tracks are drawn over the movie and stay synchronised as you scrub or play, each accepted animal in its own colour, the selected track carries a large marker and every animal is labelled, and trail length is selectable. Tracks can be edited: shift-click or lasso any number, stitch N fragments in time order, split at a frame, delete, add missing points by clicking where the animal is, and fill gaps by interpolation. Points you place carry identity ONLY - they are flagged manual_point and excluded from speed, coverage, frequency and curvature, with detected_frames and manual_points reported per track. Two new buttons set the parameters from the recording instead of from a guess: Measure a worm reads the area the detector gives one animal you click, and Mark all animals records how many there are so the review can flag when tracking finds a different number. Areas are in SOURCE pixels, so the old defaults flooded 4K recordings with noise. Opening a compressed movie no longer decodes the whole file to count frames: 122.8 s became 4.3 s on a 126 MB 4K clip for interactive paths, while analysis still forces an exact count because a blank end frame sets coverage_fraction. The spine skeleton is now selectable and recorded in analysis_metadata.json: the historical default remains, but it fragments on thick masks (no usable spine on 48% of attempted frames in a real recording) while connected thinning does not - compare both on your own recording with tools/population_swimming/compare_spine_methods.py before changing what you report. Prior: v11.115 Population swimming no longer looks frozen at "Writing results and timing report". The locomotion-modality classifier ran with no progress output and re-parsed each frame spine curvature about four times over, so on a real population it stalled silently for minutes. It now parses each frame once (identical classifications, far less work) and reports progress per track (Classifying locomotion modality: N of M), and the tool shows when the review window is being built. No classification result changed. Prior: v11.114 Small usability fixes. Supervised segmentation (the g workbench in the single-worm tracker): the threshold and scrub sliders no longer swallow the arrow keys, so Left/Right step the bad-frame preview by one source frame, PgUp/PgDn by ten, and Home/End jump to the first/last frame. Defecation: added a scope note that the tool scores the pBoc (posterior body-wall contraction, the intestinal step), not the aBoc or the expulsion step driven by the anal depressor and sphincter. Sample planner: the WINK logo now appears in the page header. No measurement changed. Prior: v11.113 Single-channel GCaMP rebuilt around three jobs. Job 1 (body-wall GCaMP): assess whether the worm body is separable from the background well enough to infer its outline, spine, and kinematics even on dim relaxed-muscle frames, then hand off to the single-worm tracker. Job 2 (a single cell): mark the soma and the process tip toward the nose, and the cell is tracked with its soma-to-tip long axis, reporting per-frame position, brightness, elongation, translational speed, and angular velocity (rotation of that axis, not the direction of travel). Job 3 (cell plus body): both at once, recording cell brightness alongside a body-trackability check. A job selector switches the numbered buttons; results export as CSV and JSON. Other tools unchanged. Prior: v11.112 Bug fixes and usability from lab testing (no biological measurement formulas changed). Defecation/pBoc: the preview and calibration frame sliders now scroll smoothly instead of sticking; the File button loads a whole numbered image sequence instead of a single frame; arrow keys and press-and-hold on the frame buttons scroll continuously; Backspace or middle-click undoes the last outline point during calibration; and a new optional worm-focus ROI lets you draw a box that follows the worm across the movie so tracking ignores other worms and distractors. The process hood now logs each step. Single-worm tracker: the open-file dialog comes to the front, and choosing the analysis interval is now a visual slider (scroll and mark start/end) instead of a text prompt. Pharyngeal pumping: the guided ROI-trajectory review (button 3b) gained a frame slider and an explicit Add-anchor-here button. Single-channel GCaMP: picking one frame of an image sequence now loads the whole folder. Mechanosensation: renamed from Evoked mechanosensation and habituation; marking stimuli now loads the whole image sequence so stimulus times can be set, plus a new What-this-does panel and an example-CSV template. Sample planner promoted to Ready. Dialogs across these tools now open in front of the window. Prior: v11.111 GitHub-based auto-update. The in-app updater can now fetch updates from the WINK GitHub releases (agvg75/WINK) when the lab L: drive is not reachable, so people running WINK off the lab network get the same one-click update prompt as lab machines. Lab machines still update from L: first; GitHub is only the fallback. No tool behaviour changed. Prior: v11.110 Pharynx morphometry and single-channel GCaMP now use the shared cockpit layout: inputs and the numbered workflow buttons on the left, a first-frame preview and status in the center, process hood on the right, with the logo theme. Their calibration, template placement, feasibility pass, extraction, neuron tracking, and review are all unchanged. This completes the migration of the safe form tools. Prior: v11.109 Three more tools moved onto the shared cockpit layout with the logo theme: Dynamic egg laying, Population tap response / habituation, and Neuromuscular paralysis pharmacology now have their inputs and buttons on the left and instructions/status in the center. Their calibration, reference-egg marking, tap detection, prod-observation review, and analysis are all unchanged. Prior: v11.108 Egg counting migrated to the shared cockpit layout: the source, frame, calibration-distance, tolerance, and worm-length fields plus the Calibrate, Draw-region, Mark-egg, and Detect/Review buttons are on the left; the chosen frame and the advanced egg-detection dials are in the center; the process hood is on the right. Calibration, ROI drawing, egg marking, detection, and the live-refresh review behave exactly as before. Prior: v11.107 The tool windows now carry the WINK logo colors too: the cockpit tools (myocyte morphometry, defecation/pBoc, population swimming, basal slowing), pharyngeal pumping, egg counting, and the shared review / ROI-drawing windows all use the slate-blue and sage-green palette with a sage accent stripe, matching the hub. This is a visual theme only - no tool behaviour changed. Prior: v11.106 Hub restyled to the WINK logo colors: the maroon is replaced by the logo slate-blue for the wordmark and headings, with a sage-green top accent stripe. Added Illinois State University under Molecular Neuroscience Lab in the brand. Individual tool windows are unchanged (neutral). Prior: v11.105 Population basal slowing now runs on the shared cockpit layout: the image folder, FPS, scale, area gates, before/after windows, buffer, and fraction inputs plus the Draw-ROIs, Undo, Clear, Analyze, and Load/Save-ROIs buttons are on the left; the first frame of the chosen folder and the status are in the center; the process hood is on the right, with the c and h panel toggles. It also gains a Calibrate scale (scope / bar) button that opens the shared in-window scale panel. ROI drawing, tracking, track review, and the paired lawn-entry review are unchanged. Close and reopen the tool to update. Prior: v11.104 made the scale calibration in-window across the cockpit tools.'
}|ConvertTo-Json|Set-Content -LiteralPath (Join-Path $Updates 'update_manifest.json') -Encoding UTF8
Remove-Item -LiteralPath $Stage -Recurse -Force
Write-Output "Built application update: $Zip"
